# Citation metadata for SNES-MDB.
#
# DRAFT — two fields need a human decision and are deliberately left as
# placeholders rather than invented:
#
#   authors  below lists the git-recorded author only. Real authorship,
#            affiliation and ORCID are not derivable from a repository and
#            must be supplied.
#   doi      absent. A DOI requires a hosting decision, which is gated on
#            the rights review for the musical corpus.
#
# `version` and `date-released` describe the CODE and the release label, not
# a published dataset. Nothing here asserts that the corpus may be
# redistributed; see LICENSE and docs/DATASET.md.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SNES-MDB, please cite both this project and NES-MDB, whose
  design, format family and composer-disjoint split convention it follows.
title: "SNES-MDB: a symbolic music database for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System"
abstract: >-
  A symbolic music corpus extracted from SNES/Super Famicom SPC files,
  intended for musical analysis and machine learning without requiring
  knowledge of SPC700 or S-DSP internals. Sample identity is resolved from
  the directory entry the S-DSP reads at key-on, so an identity is a
  property of the attack rather than of a hardware index. Uncertainty is
  published explicitly: an unestablished identity is null with a reason, and
  an unrecovered pitch is marked rather than estimated.
type: software
license: MIT
license-url: "https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html"

authors:
  - name: "SNES-MDB contributors"
    # TODO: replace with named authors, affiliations and ORCIDs.

version: "snesmdb-50game-rc1"
date-released: "2026-11-10"

keywords:
  - symbolic music
  - music information retrieval
  - Super Nintendo
  - SPC700
  - S-DSP
  - music generation
  - video game music

references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      The NES Music Database: A multi-instrumental dataset with expressive
      performance attributes
    authors:
      - family-names: Donahue
        given-names: Chris
      - family-names: Mao
        given-names: "Huanru Henry"
      - family-names: McAuley
        given-names: Julian
    collection-title: "Proceedings of the 19th International Society for Music Information Retrieval Conference (ISMIR)"
    year: 2018
  - type: software
    title: snes_spc
    authors:
      - name: "Shay Green (blargg)"
    license: LGPL-2.1
    notes: >-
      The SPC700/S-DSP emulator extraction depends on. Vendored, with three
      marked instrumentation hooks added for the research build.
